comments.body:
Pushed a commit addressing the kody-ai review on #2281:
- reasoning (`<think>`) is removed before enumerating fallback candidates, so a schema-valid example quoted there is never returned;
- the text after each fenced block (last first) is tried before the quoted blocks themselves, so a bare final answer wins over an earlier quoted example;
- fences are no longer stripped from the whole text, which corrupted fenced code inside JSON string values such as `improvedCode`;
- candidate dedupe uses a `Set`.
Added three regression tests (red before, green after).

This comment was drafted with Claude Code.

Thanks, you are right: after a fence only the first balanced value was tried, so bracketed prose like `opts[:secret]` hid the answer. Pushed 714e909f1:

- after each fence, every balanced value is now tried in order, advancing past each one (as `extractLastJsonObjectWith` does); the first that validates against the schema wins;
- new spec case with bracketed prose between the quoted block and the answer (your example); red before, green after;
- the PR description no longer mentions the removed "text with every fence removed" candidate.

This comment was drafted with Claude Code.
